# Employee salary Analysis

Problem: To understand why salary is different for employees in the company.

Data: Employee data with 474 employees. columns used: salary, starting salary, education,
experience, gender.

3 Key Insights:
1. Most employees earn between 22000 and 33000. Median salary is around 27000.
2. Salary increases with education. After 16 years of education, salary jumps from 32000 to 44000.
3. There is a gender gap. Male median salary is 32000, female median salary is 24000.

2 Recommendations:
1. Review female employee salaries and give equal pay for equal work.
2. Support education and training, and give promotion after completing degree.

Limitations:
-> Job title and department are not in the data. With that we can explain better.
-> Salary is clipped at 55000, so high salaries are not exact.